H2: Known Faults - Honda Jazz
H3: i-Shift Gearbox (2008-2015)
P: CHECK ú 2008-2015 i-Shift cars ú Get quotes by registration
P: The i-Shift, says What Car?, is best avoided because it causes the car to lurch disconcertingly whenever it changes up. FixMyCar says some 2009-2015 i-Shift models develop judder or clutch issues if servicing has been neglected. Carbuyer finds the manual gearbox the best, as the i-Shift and CVT automatics aren't particularly slick.
H3: CVT Gearbox
P: CHECK ú Older cars with a CVT ú Get quotes by registration
P: Honda dropped the i-Shift for a CVT-7 automatic gearbox in February 2011. What Car? calls it much smoother, even if it does let the engine get raucous under hard acceleration. FixMyCar says early 2001-2008 cars can suffer from CVT wear, and that some older Jazz models with a CVT can be more sensitive to gearbox wear if the transmission fluid hasn't been changed on schedule. Ask the seller for the service history of any automatic.
H3: Seized Door Locks
P: MINOR ú 2001-2008 cars ú Get quotes by registration
P: FixMyCar says early 2001-2008 cars can suffer from seized door locks. It adds that rust is often to blame, so the problem is more likely to happen as the car ages. Try each door lock before you buy.
H3: DVSA Safety Recalls
P: DVSA's recall data lists several Jazz recalls, including these. The front wide camera may not start up in the correct way after the vehicle is started. Affected vehicles may be equipped with a fuel pump module manufactured with low density impellers. The webbing sensor in the rear centre seat belt assembly could become inoperative. Driver air bag may not deploy correctly. Passenger air bag may not deploy correctly. Enter the registration in our recall check to see whether a car has a recall that is still open.
H2: Reliability Record - Honda Jazz
P: For the 2001-2008 car, What Car? calls Jazz owners "the most satisfied supermini drivers around". For the 2008-2015 car its reliability rating is 94%, and for the 2015-2020 car it is 92.4%, with What Car? adding that it is reliable and good value, too. FixMyCar says the 2016-2020 Jazz is largely trouble-free, and the latest 2020-present model remains strong.
P: In What Car?'s latest Reliability Survey, the 2020-on Jazz scored 96.9%, coming 11th out of 28 cars in the small car class. Honda as a brand scored 96.6% and finished first out of 30 brands. Carbuyer adds that when the Jazz was first included in its annual Driver Power owner satisfaction survey in 2010, it finished in 11th place overall. Which? notes that the fourth-generation Jazz, launched in 2020, is available in hybrid form only, badged Jazz e:HEV.
