H2: Known Faults - Honda Civic
P: The faults below are grouped by the years each source gives.
H3: 1.0 Petrol Wet-Belt Timing System
P: HIGH ú 2017-2022 1.0-litre petrol ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says owners of the 1.0-litre petrol model raised serious alarms regarding the wet-belt timing system. If you are looking at one, ask for the service history and ask a Honda dealer what the car's records show.
H3: Squealing Brakes
P: MINOR ú 2017-2022 ú œ372.71 average pads and discs (FixMyCar)
P: What Car? says some Civic owners have complained of squealing brakes, and that Honda is said to be aware of the problem and working on a fix. The RAC's review of the 2016-2019 car also reports a number of squeaky brakes. FixMyCar's average for replacing the brake pads and discs together is œ372.71.
H3: Diesel DPF and EGR
P: MONITOR ú 2017-2022 diesel ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says diesel owners also reported occasional DPF and EGR faults, particularly when used for short urban trips. Ask a seller how a diesel has been used.
H3: Air Conditioning and Electrics
P: CHECK ú 2017-2022 ú Get a quote
P: What Car? lists faulty air conditioning and "electrical gremlins", such as oversensitive parking sensors and glitchy infotainment screens, among the gripes across the range. The RAC mentions a few issues of electrical problems and says to check the infotainment system. What Car? adds that most repairs were handled efficiently by dealers, but out-of-warranty engine costs can be high.
H3: Diesel Oil Use
P: MONITOR ú 2006-2012 diesel ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says diesel engines can consume a lot of oil, more than one litre per 1000 miles in some cases. Check the oil level when you view one.
H3: Clutch and Dual-Mass Flywheel
P: MONITOR ú 2006-2012, about 80,000 miles ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says clutches and dual-mass flywheels can need replacing at about 80,000 miles. One Carbuyer owner of a 2007 diesel reported repeated problems with the clutch and oil pressure, plus dashboard rattles. Ask for invoices for any clutch work.
H3: Noisy Brakes, Paint and Tyre Wear
P: MINOR ú 2006-2012 ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says the main complaints on these cars were noisy brakes, imperfect paintwork and uneven tyre wear. One Carbuyer owner of a 2009 petrol reported a second-gear synchro problem and a misaligned bonnet that was still a problem.
H3: Stop/Start and Gearshift
P: MINOR ú 2015-2017 ú Get a quote
P: In the RAC's review of the 2015-2017 car, one owner complained of problems with the stop/start system, and several others reported a baulky gearshift from 2nd to 3rd. Try the stop/start and each gear on a test drive.
H3: Soft Paint
P: MINOR ú 2012-2017 and 2022 on ú Get a quote
P: On the 2012-2017 car, What Car? says some owners have found the paintwork to be quite soft, so look for excessive stone chips on the bonnet and front bumper. The RAC adds that a few customers reckoned the paintwork scratched easily. On the 2022-on car, Auto Express says some owners have found that the paint chips a bit too readily.
H3: Hybrid System Warning Light
P: MINOR ú 2022 on ú Fixed under warranty
P: In What Car?'s survey of the 2022-on car, only one car experienced a mechanical issue, a faulty hybrid system warning light, and the dealer resolved it promptly under warranty. Auto Express says the infotainment software needs to be kept up to date.
H3: DVSA Safety Recalls
P: DVSA's recall data lists several Civic recalls, including these.
LI: On affected vehicles the alloy steel bushes may be missing in all five positions of the alloy wheel.
LI: On affected vehicles due to manufacturing issues the high pressure fuel pump could leak.
LI: On affected vehicles the Hybrid HV battery may develop a fault where battery electrolyte leakage occurs that may result in a vehicle fire in a worst-case scenario.
LI: On affected vehicles after cancelling the ACC (Adaptive Cruise Control) the ISA (Intelligent Speed Assistance) will not alert the driver when over speed.
P: Enter the registration in our recall check to see whether a car has a recall that is still open.
