H2: Known Faults - Honda Accord
H3: Diesel Particulate Filter
P: MONITOR ú 2008-2015 ú Get a quote
P: Autocar's buying guide says that if a diesel has done abnormally low mileage, take it for an extended test drive checking for running issues, perhaps caused by a clogged diesel particulate filter (DPF). It adds that this is potentially very serious because cleaning the DPF can confuse the ECU, which then triggers the warning light again.
H3: EGR Pipe and Head Gasket
P: CHECK ú 2008-2015 ú Get a quote
P: Autocar says to check for white smoke, possibly caused by a failed head gasket, and to examine the exhaust gas recirculation pipe for cracks.
H3: Clutch
P: MONITOR ú 2008-2015 ú Get a quote
P: Autocar says manual diesels can suffer premature clutch slip, so boot it from second and see how it likes it. A Carbuyer owner review of a 2009 2.0 EX diesel says the clutch needed replacement at less than 50000 miles.
H3: Dual-Mass Flywheel
P: CHECK ú 2008-2015 ú Get a quote
P: According to Autocar, a rattle when pulling away or a series of loud clunks could be the dual mass flywheel breaking up.
H3: Fuel Filter
P: MONITOR ú 2008-2015 ú Get a quote
P: That Carbuyer owner also reported that a couple of times the diesel engine went into a "limp mode" with reduced power, due to fuel filter clogging between services.
H3: Diesel Low-Oil Warning
P: HIGH ú 2002-2008 ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says the diesel engine likes a regular pint of oil, and there's no dash light to warn you that the engine is running dry. It adds that there is a tell-tale to warn if the pressure has dropped, but by the time that lights, you may have mangled the engine.
H3: Cabin Trim and Electronics
P: MINOR ú 2008-2015 ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says stereo issues and temperamental Bluetooth phone systems have been mentioned on the 2008-2015 Accord, but the biggest reported concern is cabin trim and build quality.
H3: DVSA Safety Recalls
P: DVSA's recall data lists several Accord recalls, including these.
LI: Abnormal deployment pressure may lead to rupture of the passenger's air bag inflator case.
LI: Abnormal deployment pressure may lead to rupture of the inflator case.
LI: The subject vehicles are equipped with front passenger airbag inflators which could have been assembled with improperly manufactured propellant wafers.
LI: Due to an inappropriate software setting of the Engine Control Unit the oil level in the engine may increase due to fuel dilution during the Diesel Particulate Filter (DPF) regeneration.
LI: The fuel pump relay may fail which will result in either the engine not starting or stalling.
P: Check whether a car has an open recall with our recall check .
H2: Reliability Survey Results - Honda Accord
P: What Car? says that for the 2008-2015 Accord, Honda always does well in customer satisfaction and reliability surveys, and the Accord upholds this tradition. It topped the family car category of the 2010 JD Power survey, and came fifth overall.
P: For the 2002-2008 Accord, What Car? says Honda has earned itself a regular top-five slot in the What Car? Reliability Index, while owners responding to the JD Power Survey praised their cars to the skies.
H3: Honda as a Brand
P: In Auto Express's Driver Power 2026 table of the most and least reliable car brands, Honda, as a brand, came fourth with 90.31%.
