H2: Known Faults - Honda CR-V
H3: Hybrid System Warnings
P: MONITOR ú 2018-2023 ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says some owners of the 2018-2023 CR-V reported problems with the hybrid system, including warning lights appearing unexpectedly and an occasional loss of power. Look at the dashboard for warning lights when you view a car, and ask for the service history.
H3: Infotainment System
P: MONITOR ú 2018-2023 ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says other owners of the 2018-2023 CR-V mentioned faults with the infotainment system, such as freezing screens and Bluetooth connectivity issues, though these were often resolved with software updates. Pair your phone and use the screen for a few minutes on a test drive.
H3: Electrical Fault
P: MONITOR ú 2018-2023 ú Get a quote
P: One owner told What Car? that they needed multiple visits to resolve an electrical fault on their 2018-2023 CR-V. Work through the windows, locks and lights before you buy.
H3: Fuel Pump Module
P: CHECK ú 2018-2023 ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says an issue has been found with the fuel pump module on CR-Vs manufactured from the start of production up until 5 March 2019. Ask a Honda dealer whether the car you are looking at is affected.
H3: Rear Light Clusters
P: MONITOR ú 2007-2012 ú Get a quote
P: Carbuyer's buying guide to the 2007-2012 CR-V says to check for rear light clusters that look foggy inside, as water ingress is quite common.
H3: Air Conditioning Compressor
P: CHECK ú 2007-2012 ú Get a quote
P: Carbuyer says air-conditioning compressors can break on the 2007-2012 CR-V, so make sure the air blows as cold as you would expect. Run the system for a few minutes on a test drive.
H3: Door Handle Paint
P: MINOR ú 2007-2012 ú Get a quote
P: For the 2007-2012 CR-V, Carbuyer says to check the door handles for flaking silver paint.
H3: DVSA Safety Recalls
P: DVSA's recall data lists several CR-V recalls, including these.
LI: Affected vehicles may have been fitted with an incorrectly labelled trailer hitch of the wrong specification which may come into contact with the Integrated Power Unit (IPU) when a rear-end collision occurs and result in a short circuit in the high-voltage power system or a risk of fire.
LI: In certain collisions the cable may be pinched between the body and the collision object and may be damaged.
LI: Power window switch can accumulate water causing overheat and possible fire.
LI: The propellant used in the air bag inflators may degrade over time due to heat cycles and exposure to moisture.
P: Check any car you are considering by its registration in our recall check .
