H2: Known Faults - Honda HR-V
P: The faults below come from used-car reviews of the 2015 to 2021 HR-V and from owners. The newest car, on sale from 2021, is hybrid only, and it has its own section further down.
H3: Build Quality and Trim
P: MONITOR ú 2015-2021 ú Get a quote
P: The RAC says build quality from the Mexican factory is not always great on the 2015-2018 car, so check for slightly wobbly fixtures and fittings, plus various creaks and rattles. For the 2019-2021 car it reports poor paint quality, loose window gaskets and poorly fitted body panels. One Carbuyer owner said the quality was shocking, with plastics actually falling off. That is one owner's experience, not a survey result.
H3: Clutch
P: CHECK ú 2015-2018 ú Get a quote
P: The RAC mentions one owner who needed to replace the clutch, and suggests checking the gear shift action. This is a single report, so treat it as a reason to test the gearbox on a drive rather than as a known pattern.
H3: Engine Management Fault
P: MONITOR ú 2015-2018 ú Get a quote
P: The RAC also came across reports of an engine management fault on the 2015-2018 car. It gives no more detail, so ask a seller whether any warning light has come on and what was done about it.
H3: Electrical Sensors and Infotainment
P: CHECK ú 2019-2021 ú Get a quote
P: For the 2019-2021 car the RAC reports electric sensor issues and says to examine all of the car's electrical features. It adds that there have been reported issues with the infotainment system, so make sure it works as it should before you buy.
H3: Side Steps and Roof Bars
P: MINOR ú 2015-2021 ú Get a quote
P: The RAC has come across corroding side steps and delaminating roof bars on the 2019-2021 car. A Carbuyer owner said the side steps on their car had been replaced twice due to corrosion. If a car you are viewing has either fitted, look at them closely.
H3: Stop-Start
P: MINOR ú 2015-2020 ú Get a quote
P: One Carbuyer owner of a 2015-2020 car said they had nothing but problems with the stop start function. Again this is one person's report. On a test drive, stop at a junction and watch how the system behaves.
H3: Adaptive Cruise Control
P: MINOR ú 2021 on (hybrid) ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says the newest HR-V is only available as a hybrid and that its reliability is looking good. Autocar called its long-term hybrid HR-V well built and entirely reliable. Its writer did say that the adaptive cruise control had freaked out at a parked car, a shadow or seemingly nothing at all. That is the experience of one car, so try the system on the road if the car you are viewing has it.
H3: DVSA Safety Recalls
P: DVSA's recall data lists these HR-V recalls. Affected vehicles may be equipped with a fuel pump module manufactured with low density impellers. The webbing sensor in the rear centre seat belt assembly could become inoperative. The regulatory requirement for emissions levels are not met. Enter the registration in our recall check to see whether a car has a recall that is still open.
